# Testing rules

Source: `docs/architecture/ARCHITECTURE.md` §10, §12.

- Each acceptance test carries its ID: pytest `@pytest.mark.trace("AT-M0-T03-02", reqs=["ARCH-R031"])`; Vitest and Playwright titles start with `[AT-…]`. (Checked: `make trace-report`.)
- Expected values come only from `tests/fixtures/golden/` or `tests/fixtures/metrics/`. Never compute expectations with the code under test; never hard-code an expected business number in test code.
- Tests are deterministic: frozen `as_of`, fixed seeds, derandomized Hypothesis in CI, `TZ=UTC` with explicit Asia/Riyadh assertions, no external network (`pytest-socket`), no live model.
- Unit tests touch no database or network. Integration tests use the test database with rollback or app-schema truncation. E2E runs on the Compose stack.
- Test both success and refusal: authorization denial, empty scope, unavailable, partial and error states.
- Never skip, `xfail` or loosen a failing test to get green. Quarantine needs `DEF-nnnn`, an expiry within 7 days and the owner's approval. (Checked: quarantine expiry lint.)
- Live-model tests run only via `make agent-test-live` or `eval-live.yml`, with budgets.
- Every Playwright journey runs axe-core on each state it visits.
